Assembler Version 09
====================
Assembled by: version 08 (instgen assembled by v06, asm assembled by v08)

Features Supported by This Assembler
-------------------------------------
Same feature set as version 08, with line number tracking in error messages
and stderr output:

Syntax:
- Non-standard (custom) mnemonic syntax: LDA#, LDAZ, STAZ, etc.
- DATA pseudo-instruction for raw byte emission
- Hex constants: $xx (1 byte) or $xxxx (2 bytes)
- Quoted strings with \n escape
- Label definitions with PC value or explicit assignment
- PC setting via: * = $xxxx (with zero-fill on pass 2)
- Low byte (<) and high byte (>) operators on labels
- Relative branch (~label) syntax (also auto-detected via flags)
- Labels as 2-byte operands
- Comments with semicolons
- Two-pass assembly
- Flag-based operand type detection
- Zero page addressing with plain hex values

Instruction set: same as version 07/08

Error handling: same errors as version 08 (errors 1-A), plus:
- Error messages now include line number
- Error messages written to stderr via write_d
- Format: "Error N at line M: message"
- Decimal number conversion for line numbers

New in this version (relative to version 08):
- Error messages written to stderr (write_d at $F00C) instead of via BRK message
- Line number tracking used in error output (CURLINEL/CURLINEH incremented per line)
- Decimal number formatting (to_decimal routine) for displaying line numbers
- Custom interrupt handler that formats error messages with error code and line number
- Exit via dedicated exit vector ($F00F) instead of BRK $00
- Reset vector at $FFFC and interrupt vector at $FFFE
- show_message and show_decimal helper routines for stderr output
- BRK still used to trigger errors, but the interrupt handler formats the output

